<h2>What I Do</h2>
<p>
  I write code that's cleaner than my diet (which is saying something—I actually enjoy kale chips). From React frontends to Python backends, I craft digital experiences while keeping one eye on performance metrics and the other on carbon footprints. My technical toolkit includes everything from neural networks to memory allocators, because why choose between AI and low-level systems when you can have both?
</p>

<h2>My Philosophy</h2>
<p>
  Code should be like renewable energy: efficient, sustainable, and not a burden on future generations. I'm passionate about building technology that doesn't just solve today's problems but does so in a way that doesn't create tomorrow's environmental headaches. Whether it's optimizing algorithms or optimizing my morning smoothie recipe, I believe in thoughtful engineering—and yes, I definitely overthink both.
</p> 